# Private working files — must never end up in the public GitHub repo.
# These contain prospect lists with personal contact info, draft emails
# with details about specific recipients, etc. Adding to .gitignore at
# the repo root so they're invisible to git regardless of subdirectory.

PROSPECTS.md
PROSPECTS-*.md
private/
*.private.md

# Claude Code local harness files — local settings + runtime locks.
# Never belong in the repo.
.claude/

# Secrets — never commit any .env variant, even accidentally.
# The real secrets store lives OUTSIDE this repo at
# C:\BUSINESS\PHASEWISE\phasewise-secrets\ — this is belt-and-suspenders
# in case something ever gets copied into the repo tree by mistake.
.env
.env.*
.env.local
*.env
hunter.env
loops.env
stripe*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# Secrets folders — same defense against accidental repo copies.
phasewise-secrets/
.phasewise-secrets/
secrets/
.secrets/

# Prospect data — contains personal contact info, personalization notes with
# analytical shorthand, Caltrans-overlap warnings, and Kevin-specific decision
# annotations. Never belongs in the public repo, even under phasewise/phasewise.
automation/prospects*.csv
prospects*.csv
PROSPECTS-*.csv
